{{nihongo|'''Hōtō'''|ほうとう|}} is a [[noodle soup]] and popular [[regional cuisine|regional dish]] originating from [[Yamanashi Prefecture|Yamanashi]], [[Japan]] made by stewing flat [[udon]] noodles and [[vegetable]]s in [[miso soup]]. Though ''hōtō'' is commonly recognized as a variant of ''[[udon]]'', locals do not consider it to be an ''udon'' dish because the dough is prepared in the style of dumplings rather than noodles.
